<title>ITALY: Italian Dec industrial turnover up 0.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Italian Dec industrial turnover up 0.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian industrial turnover rose 0.6 percent year on year in December, while orders fell 5.9 percent, national statistics institute ISTAT said.</p>
<p>    INDUSTRIAL TURNOVER   Dec 1996     Nov 1996     Dec 1995</p>
<p>    Year on year change   +0.6	   -8.4 pct     +5.8</p>
<p>    Index (100= 1990)     146.1	  139.1	  145.2</p>
<p>    -Domestic demand	-1.4	   -10.4 pct    +7.1</p>
<p>    -Foreign demand	 +5.7	   -3.4 pct     +2.5</p>
<p>INDUSTRIAL ORDERS</p>
<p>    Year on year change   -5.9	   -10.3 pct    +1.0</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)     137.7	  131.2	  146.3</p>
<p>    -Domestic demand	-8.9	  -12.5 pct     -3.5</p>
<p>    -Foreign demand	 -1.0	   -6.8 pct     +9.1</p>
<p>Note: Istat said the rise in turnover was especially marked in the mining and minerals sector (+68.7 percent) and petrol (+11.8 percent) while leather goods fell 10.8 percent and metal fell 9.8 percent.</p>
<p>For orders, the biggest rises were in textiles and clothing (+20.7 percent) and furniture (+12.6 percent) while the transport sector fell 25.3 percent and leather goods fell 14.4 percent.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
